  I think a better classing is like the following, since here the sharding is on Dbuffer instead of a single tensor:
  class DBufferShard(Placement):
      """Base for DBuffer-internal dim-0 shard placements; not a DTensor Shard."""
      def to_dtensor_placement(self) -> Shard:
          return Shard(0)

  class Flat(DBufferShard): ...
  class BlockAtomic(DBufferShard): ...
  class TensorAtomic(DBufferShard): ...

but, this seems out of range of this PR.
